{
 "id": "eu-checkout",
 "question": "Why does checkout fail for EU customers?",
 "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
 "recorded": "2026-10-20",
 "answer": "EU checkout most likely fails because the shop's EU One Stop Shop (OSS) VAT registration number isn't configured, so the VAT lookup refuses to return a rate.\n\n**How it fails:**\n\n1. `shop/config.py`: `OSS_ID = os.environ.get(\"SHOP_OSS_ID\", \"\")` falls back to an empty string when the `SHOP_OSS_ID` environment variable isn't set.\n2. `shop.tax.vat_rate`: for an EU country (`shop.countries.is_eu`), if `config.OSS_ID` is empty it logs `tax.no_registration` and raises `shop.errors.TaxRegistrationError`. It deliberately doesn't guess a rate. US orders and orders outside the EU never reach this check, which is why only EU customers are affected.\n3. `TaxRegistrationError` is a subclass of `PricingError`. In `shop.checkout.place_order`, the error from `pricing.total(cart, customer)` is caught, logged as `checkout.pricing_failed`, and re-raised as `CheckoutFailed(\"pricing_unavailable\")`. This happens before any stock is reserved or any card is charged.\n\nI didn't open `shop.pricing.total` itself. That it reaches `vat_rate` is an inference from the graph, where `pricing.total` is listed as a caller, and from `docs/vat.md`.\n\n**What to check:** look for `tax.no_registration` warnings and `checkout.pricing_failed` events with reason `pricing_unavailable` in the logs. If they're there, set `SHOP_OSS_ID` in the deployment environment and restart. The config is read once at import, so a restart is needed. `docs/runbooks/oss-registration.md` covers getting and deploying the number, and `docs/vat.md` and `docs/adr/0007-destination-vat.md` explain why EU orders need it.",
